Controller -> Handles requests/responses
- Handles HTTP requests (from frontend or external clients)
- Entry point for REST API

Service -> Contains business logic
- Contains business logic (think of it as model)
- Controllers call services, and services handle the "thinking"

Repository -> Talks to the database
- Talks directly to the database
- Extends Spring Data JPA's JpaRepository

Entity -> Represents database tables
- Defines the database tables as Java classes
- Fields map to table columns
@Entity
class Book {
    @Id
    Long id;
    ...
}

DTO (Data Transfer Object) -> Defines data shape for API
- Represents data sent between backend <--> frontend
- Prevents exposing entity details (e.g. passwords)
- Usually used in controllers and services

Config -> Holds configuration
- Store configuration classes (CORS, security, beans, etc..)

Frontend -> Controller -> Service -> Repository -> Entity -> SQL Database (H2/Postgres)
React    REST API layer   Model      db access     db table    db


